      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I've verified this behavior by repeatedly running wget on a malformed FieldSearch query against the REST api using wget: </p>\n\n<p>wget <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/fedora/objects?pid=true&amp;query=label%3D%3F&amp;maxResults=20\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/fedora/objects?pid=true\\&amp;query=label%3D%3F\\&amp;maxResults=20</a></p>\n\n<p>It looks like a connection is borrowed from the pool, and when the query fails in this way, the connection is not immediately released as it should be.  If this is done many times in a row, eventually the connection pool will be exhausted and will cause Fedora to block (hang) on subsequent requests.</p>",
     "created": "04/Feb/10 6:56 PM",
     "id": "11227",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10563/comment/11227",
